  "entryPoint": "AnalyzeRule.getString/getStringList (default and URL modes)",
  "expectationSource": "Derived by reading the frozen AnalyzeByJSoup.kt, AnalyzeRule.kt and jsoup 1.16.2 at the pinned commit. The frozen APK run that turns these rows into device goldens is not-run; see README.md. Ticket #11 added the four `path: \"rule\"` cases: their rule carries an `@js:` segment, a `<js>` block, a `{{baseUrl}}` interpolation and the always-null `{{title}}` binding, and the golden must run them through the same `AnalyzeRule.getString` entry with `setContent(html, baseUrl)`, so `baseUrl` is the committed `http://fixture.test` above. The destination side of those cases is the product rule-field path (`lib/source/rule_field.dart` in front of the Rust adapter), not the bare adapter, which is what the `rule` path tells `tool/html_adapter_gate.dart` to run. Ticket #51 corrected one expectation: `replacement-trailing-field` was read from a Java-style split of `##`, but the frozen `SourceRule.makeUpRule` (`AnalyzeRule.kt:686-695`) uses Kotlin's `split(\"##\")`, whose default `limit` of zero keeps the trailing empty field, so that rule is the frozen `replaceFirst`; `AnalyzeRule.replaceRegex` (`:426-437`) then answers with the replaced match only, `忘语先生`, which the handset returns.",
